**The Equations and Equilibums**

When H2S is added to a solution containing metal2+ ions, the following reaction occurs:

```
M2+ + S2- → M2S (M = Mn, Cu, Hg, Ni)
```

The solubility of the M2S will depend on the concentration of the metal2+ and the degree-of-equilibrium.

