","Here here the classifications of each study:

*   **a. Retrospective:** This study uses past data (past smoking history) to explore a current outcome ( bladder cancer). It's looking into past events to understand current factors.

*   ****b. Cross-sectional:** The study examines a population (nurses) at a single-time point. It's examining multiple variables (eating habits and health) simultaneously.

*   **c. Prospective:** This study follows a group of people over a period of time, tracking their health and potential-related factors (eating and exercise) to see if it increases the risk of developing cancer.

*   **d. Cross-survey:** This study compares two-of-other-equal factors (generic and named-based products) at a single time period.",relevance,"# Task Description
