<USER_REQUEST>
State whether each study is cross-sectional, retrospective, or prospective.  

a) To see if there is a link between smoking and bladder cancer, patients with bladder cancer are asked if they currently smoke or if they smoked in the past.  
b) The Nurses Health Survey was a survey where nurses were asked to record their eating habits over a period of time, and their general health was recorded.  
c) A new study is underway to track the eating and exercise patterns of people at different time-periods in the future, and see who is afflicted with cancer later in life.  
d) The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
Here here the classifications of each study:

*   **a. Retrospective:** This study uses past data (past smoking history) to explore a current outcome ( bladder cancer). It's looking into past events to understand current factors.

*   ****b. Cross-sectional:** The study examines a population (nurses) at a single-time point. It's examining multiple variables (eating habits and health) simultaneously.

*   **c. Prospective:** This study follows a group of people over a period of time, tracking their health and potential-related factors (eating and exercise) to see if it increases the risk of developing cancer.

*   **d. Cross-survey:** This study compares two-of-other-equal factors (generic and named-based products) at a single time period.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

